{"c":[{"name":"20261022T175949Z-e9f28fbf7dbe5041","text":"2026-10-22: live data has many identical vectors (one query: 150 owners at distance 0), so top-k ties at the cut are common; exact semantic breaks them by harness, then id. DuckDB Python draws a progress bar on stdout for long queries; SET enable_progress_bar = false to parse it.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261022T183706Z-584e9a2f3117f291","text":"DuckDB 2.0.0 nanobind 'leaked instances' at exit of embed/semantic: stockroom's own HF Hub logger filter (_DropUnauthenticatedHubWarning) stays on the logger for the process; its class pins stockroom.embed globals, so duckdb. Removing it after model load: no warning (2026-10-22).","type":"note"}]}
